<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) (Euplectella aspergillum)",
        "Euplectella aspergillum Turing wavenumber at 34.3 µm (Holocene, detail s0) faithfully reproduces Euplectella aspergillum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Euplectella aspergillum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-euplectella-aspergillum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Euplectella aspergillum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A chronospecies split. Holocene only, 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/1.",
        "does_not_claim: That Monn et al. 2015 lamella thicknesses were fitted, or that a second specimen was scored.",
        "does_not_claim: That the image radial Pearson exceeded 0.98. It is 0.948.",
        "does_not_claim: That this sponge has ocelli or pigment stripes.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ablation, γ sweep, specimen-crop Pearson, RMSE, and KS.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Four-mode amplitude equations on |k|=k_c, drawn with a fixed reference radius.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg linearisation and σ(k), calibrated to λ_c=3.43e-05 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Aizenberg et al. 2005: seven hierarchical levels and a cylindrical square lattice reinforced by diagonal ridges.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: dispersion relation and critical wavenumber.",
        "reported_in_source: Weaver et al. 2007: assembly of the siliceous lattice of E. aspergillum.",
        "transfer_boundary: Cohort wording 'pigment stripe / ocellus' names a skeletal-lattice wavelength. The portrait magnifies λ_c." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Euplectella aspergillum (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
